Package: adlaplace
Type: Package
Title: Laplace Approximations Using Automatic Differentiation
Version: 0.7.3
Date: 2026-09-28
Authors@R: person(given="Patrick", family="Brown", email="patrick.borgnine@gmail.com", role=c("aut","cre","cph"))
Maintainer: Patrick Brown <patrick.borgnine@gmail.com>
Description: Computes Laplace-approximate maximum likelihood for hierarchical
    and latent Gaussian models. A formula interface specifies observation
    densities (Gaussian, Poisson, binomial, negative binomial, and
    Dirichlet-multinomial) and random terms (independent effects and
    integrated Wiener process smooths) together with fixed effects. Random
    effects are maximized by a sparse trust-region method whose gradient and
    Hessian come from automatic differentiation with 'CppAD'; fixed effects
    and variance components are then estimated from the Laplace profile
    likelihood and its profile gradient. The Laplace log-determinant uses a
    sparse selected inverse. Optional post-fit tools include adaptive
    Gauss-Hermite quadrature ('aghq') and approximate maximum influence
    perturbations. Methods follow Tierney and Kadane (1986)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1986.10478240>, Kristensen, Nielsen, Berg, Skaug,
    and Bell (2016) <doi:10.18637/jss.v070.i05>, Braun (2014)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v060.i04>, Rue and Held (2005, ISBN:9781584884323),
    Stringer, Brown, and Stafford (2022)
    <doi:10.1080/10618600.2022.2099403>, Bilodeau, Stringer, and Tang (2022)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2022.2141635>, Broderick, Giordano, and Meager
    (2023) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2011.14999>, 'CppAD'
    <https://github.com/coin-or/CppAD>, and Erisman and Tinney (1975)
    <doi:10.1145/360680.360704>.
